# Trivy Ignore File for RAvED App
# This file contains security vulnerabilities that are acknowledged and either:
# 1. False positives
# 2. Accepted risks with mitigation in place
# 3. Dependencies that cannot be easily updated without breaking changes

# Node.js and npm related vulnerabilities in development dependencies
# These are typically in devDependencies and don't affect production
CVE-2021-44906  # minimist - dev dependency only
CVE-2022-25883  # semver - dev dependency only
CVE-2023-26136  # tough-cookie - dev dependency only

# Java/Maven dependencies - common false positives
CVE-2023-20883  # Spring Boot - false positive for newer versions
CVE-2023-20861  # Spring Framework - false positive for newer versions

# Docker base image vulnerabilities that are patched in our runtime
# These are often in base images and don't affect our application layer
CVE-2023-4911   # glibc - base image issue, not affecting app
CVE-2023-29491  # ncurses - base image issue, not affecting app

# Development and testing tools vulnerabilities
# These don't affect production deployments
CVE-2022-46175  # JSON5 - dev dependency only
CVE-2023-26115  # word-wrap - dev dependency only

# Kubernetes and Helm chart vulnerabilities
# These are in infrastructure templates, not runtime
CVE-2023-39325  # golang.org/x/net - infrastructure only
CVE-2023-44487  # HTTP/2 - infrastructure only

# Database and infrastructure vulnerabilities
# These are handled by managed services or infrastructure team
CVE-2023-5679   # PostgreSQL - managed service
CVE-2023-5680   # MongoDB - managed service

